{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"Issue #396 requires ACP backends to configure arbitrary per-variable plain and secret environment values while preserving schema validation and config redaction.","decision":"Added explicit dynamic key families to the backend settings schema, constrained members to environment-variable names, kept family storage tied to isSecret, and merged accepted ACP values into the launch environment without logging values.","impact":"Literal schemas remain supported; generic config setters list and validate dynamic keys; ACP launch configuration now includes secret values held from backend.secrets; no process launch or ACP Turn behavior was added.","recurrence_control":"Regression tests cover dynamic writes, invalid and unrelated keys, storage separation, redaction, launch environment composition, duplicate rejection, and secret-safe diagnostics.","rejected_alternatives":["Allow unknown keys for every registered backend, which would remove typo detection for literal schemas."],"sources":[]}
